      "writtenOn": "2025-02-06T21:37:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks `k_sleep()` and others are only woken up by `k_wakeup()`.  Our Zephyr code has no references to `k_wakeup()`, and upstream I only see this called from some tests and one driver.\n\nSo I think we\u0027re safe to use `k_sleep()` as a direct replacement for `crec_sleep()`",
